smartinit.v4.2.0

June 2018 NAM smartinit changes to coincide with RTMA/URMA v2.7 upgrade (see docs/README for more details on changes)

* NAM nest will be used at 00 H instead of NAM parent for Puerto Rico and Hawaii.

* Total cloud cover bugfix - at 00 H, the total cloud cover field is written out for CONUS and Alaska.  Previously,
  0.0's were written for total cloud cover.

* Added fields needed for VIIRS land surface temperature data assimilation in RTMA/URMA for Alaska only.
        -pressure, temperature, mixing ratio, u, v, height at model level 1
        -pressure, temperature, and mixing ratio at model level 2
        -surface roughness

* Changed the decimal precision of downscaled specific humidity to 6.0
* Changed the decimal precision of downscaled surface pressure to 6.0
* Changed the decimal precision of wind gust to -4.0
* Changed the decimal precision of visibility to 3.0

#===============================================================================
 IMPLEMENTATION INSTRUCTIONS 
#===============================================================================

1.  git clone -b tags/RB-v4.2.0 ssh://${USER}@vlab.ncep.noaa.gov:29418/EMC_smartinit smartinit.v4.2.0

    to set up and run on WCOSS phase 2.

2.  Copy fixed files to the fix directory

    cp -r /meso2/noscrub/Annette.Gibbs/emc-binaries/smartinit/fix smartinit.v4.2.0

2.  Build sorc codes smartinit_g2.fd, smartprecip_g2.fd
       
	The modulefile used for the build is in modulefiles/SMARTINIT/v4.2.0.  Copy it to a location from which it can
	be loaded (/nwprod2/modulefiles/SMARTINIT or something similar). 

	In the smartinit sorc directory "smartinit.v4.2.0/sorc" type
		./build_smartinit.scr
	to compile the codes sequentially.  All executables will be copied over to the smartinit "exec" directory.

4.  Use ...docs/smartinit.ver file if desired to set
      model_ver=v4.2.0  parameter

5.  I recommend you remove the following directories, as they are no longer needed or used:

	ecf/sminit_ak
	ecf/sminit_conus
	ecf/sminit_dgex-ak
	ecf/sminit_dgex-cs 

    The CONUS (5km), Alaska (6km) and ak_rtmages (6 km) and DGEX smartinits are no longer needed or used.

6.  Job Dependencies: 
     Upstream: NAM/NAM Nest, SREF; 
     Upstream links:

     NAM/NAM Nest 
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.bgrd3d${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.priconest.bsmart${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.hawaiinest.bsmart${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.conusnest.bsmart${hh}.tm00
     /com2/nam/prod/nam.$PDY/nam.t${cyc}z.alaskanest.bsmart${hh}.tm00

     SREF
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/${hh}/ensprod/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb212.prob_3hrly
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/${hh}/ensprod/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb243.prob_3hrly
     /com2/sref/prod/sref.$PDY/${hh}/ensprod/sref.t${hh}z.pgrb216.prob_3hrly

     Downstream: RTMA, URMA
     Downstream links(J-Jobs that use NAM smartinit files): 

     /nwprod2/rtma.v2.7.0/jobs/JRTMA_GETGUESS
     /nwprod2/urma.v2.7.0/jobs/JURMA_GETGUESS

7.  Test plan: 

	Test J-Jobs jobs/JNAM_SMINIT for a full 24-hour period.

8.  Technical Details:
	Runtime: ~3 hours, 30 minutes wallclock
	Nodes: 12
	Tasks per node: 12
	Consumable memory: 4916 mb
	Serial vs parallel: Parallel (wgrib2 only)
	Disk Storage: Has decreased by 21.4 GB total (removed all GRIB1, conus (5km), alaska (6km), and ak_rtmages (6km) files)

7.  New output files: None

8.  Flow Diagram:

    https://drive.google.com/a/noaa.gov/file/d/0B7IqRnJWIYHlaVhCcUdaQ1RaZzQ/view?usp=sharing

NOTE: Details on all changes to nam smartinit are found at docs/README - Search for 4.2.0 for changes related to this implemenation.

